BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (standard package, and custom studies for transit-planning projects at $15,000 to $30,000.) Tj T* (Universities can fund these from sustainability budgets, parking and transportation revenue, or) Tj T* (green-fee funds, which several campuses already administer for exactly this purpose. Our) Tj T* (commuter-facing app is free, so adoption is not constrained by individual willingness to pay.) Tj T* (We estimate gross margin at 78 percent for licenses and 55 percent for advisory work, and a) Tj T* (customer acquisition cost of about $4,000 per campus, recovered within the first contract year.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (Campus transportation surveys offered by consulting firms are slow, costly at $15,000 to) Tj T* ($40,000 per cycle, and low in response. Corporate commute-management platforms focus on parking) Tj T* (and employee benefits rather than emissions reporting, and do not serve student populations.) Tj T* (Consumer carbon-footprint apps lack institutional dashboards and rely on self-reported trips.) Tj T* (Transit agencies collect ridership data but nothing on trips they do not carry. No competitor) Tj T* (we found combines passive trip measurement, behavior-change recommendations and reporting) Tj T* (designed for campus climate commitments. Our advantage is reinforced by our data: each enrolled) Tj T* (campus improves our mode-detection accuracy and our estimates of the impact of each type of) Tj T* (intervention.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Priya Raghunathan, chief executive, is a senior in environmental economics who managed our) Tj T* (university's student sustainability fund and led the commuter-survey redesign that raised) Tj T* (campus response from 11 to 19 percent. Marcus Delacroix-Whitfield, chief technology officer, is) Tj T* (a computer science senior who built the trip-detection engine and previously interned on a) Tj T* (mobile data team, shipping a location-based feature used by 200,000 people. Tomasz Okonkwo-) Tj T* (Nowak, head of partnerships, is a master's student in urban planning who spent two years) Tj T* (working with the regional transit authority on service-gap analysis. Our faculty advisor in the) Tj T* (sustainability institute has overseen three campus emissions inventories.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have formed Greenlight Commute LLC and defined the core product concept and data model. Our) Tj T* (pilot on our own campus enrolled 1,840 commuters over one semester, 11 percent of the commuting) Tj T* (population, and signed two paid agreements: a $6,000 annual license with our university's) Tj T* (sustainability office and a $9,500 advisory engagement with a neighboring college. Among pilot) Tj T* (participants who received switch plans, solo-driving trips fell 14 percent relative to a) Tj T* (matched group over twelve weeks, avoiding an estimated 21 metric tons of carbon dioxide. Early) Tj T* (projections: $15,500 in booked revenue this year, rising to $190,000 in year two with eight) Tj T* (campuses and $720,000 in year three with twenty-five. We expect to reach breakeven during year) Tj T* (three, with costs driven mainly by two engineers, a part-time analyst and cloud infrastructure.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Ask For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are seeking a $25,000 prize or seed grant to fund our next twelve months: roughly $12,000 to) Tj T* (harden the app's trip detection and privacy architecture, $8,000 to convert six campuses now in) Tj T* (conversation from pilot discussions to signed contracts, and $5,000 for legal review of data-) Tj T* (protection agreements. We would also value introductions to campus sustainability networks and) Tj T* (mentorship from judges experienced in selling to higher education. With this support, we will) Tj T* (have eight paying campuses and a repeatable sales process by the end of next year.) Tj ET
